#DESCRIPTION
Hybrid PIC (kinetic ions / fluid electrons) 1D PERIODIC CONVECTION-TERM test
on a TRUE 1D grid (32x1x1 cells), run for exactly ONE ADVECTION PERIOD.
Isolates the convection term of the generalized Ohm's law, E = -U_i x B.
The Hall term, resistivity, and electron-pressure-gradient are OFF, so with a
uniform bulk flow U the induction equation reduces to ideal advection,
  dB/dt = -U . grad B,
and a seeded transverse (By, Bz) wave is advected rigidly at the bulk speed.

TESTCASE ConvectionWave seeds the transverse wave via fill_hybrid_wave(0.2)
(B1 = 0.2*Bx0) with NO velocity perturbation, and UNIFORMSTATE sets a uniform
bulk flow ux = 10 km/s. The guide field Bx0 = 5.2195e-11 T (~0.01 in code
units) is chosen DELIBERATELY WEAK so the field is dynamically PASSIVE:
v_A_code ~ 0.01 << U_code = 0.2 and Omega_i*T_code ~ 0.05 << 1, so the kinetic
ions cannot react on the run time scale (a delta-B seed with no matching
delta-u on a strong field would instead split into counter-propagating
Alfven/cyclotron branches and NOT advect rigidly).

NOTE ON TIME UNITS: TIMESTEPPING dt, SAVEPLOT dt and STOP TimeMax are in SI
seconds, while phase speeds are per CODE time unit; tNorm = lNormSI/uNormSI =
1.0e5/5.0e4 = 2.0 s, so TimeMax = 64 s -> T_code = 32.0. The advection period
is ONE WAVELENGTH: lambda = Lx * lNormSI = 6.4 * 1.0e5 m = 640 km, and
  T_period = lambda / ux = 640 km / 10 km/s = 64 s,
exactly TimeMax, so after the run the wave has translated one full wavelength
and the (By, Bz) pattern returns to its initial shape. With Ux_code =
ux_SI/uNormSI = 1.0e4/5.0e4 = 0.2 and kx = 2*pi/Lx (Lx = 6.4), the phase at a
fixed x advances by
  Delta(phi) = -kx * Ux_code * T_code = -2*pi/6.4 * 0.2 * 32.0 = -2*pi rad
over the full run (residual Alfven contamination O(1-cos(kx*vA*T_code)) ~ 1%);
the transverse amplitude is conserved (no damping). Plots are written every
16 s (SAVEPLOT dt = 16.0), i.e. at QUARTER PERIODS (t = 0, 16, 32, 48, 64 s):
the k=1 phase advances by exactly -pi/2 between consecutive frames. The
quarter-period sampling is what makes the one-period check non-degenerate --
with only the first/last frames a full -2*pi turn wraps to 0 and would be
indistinguishable from a wave that never moved.

Validated by tests/validate_tests.py :: _check_convection_advection, which
checks (1) the -pi/2 phase advance over the shortest consecutive-frame gap
(advection at U), (2) that after the full period the first/last patterns
coincide (wrapped phase shift ~ 0), and (3) amplitude ratio in [0.7, 1.3]
(no damping or growth).

Normalization matches hybrid_whistler (lNormSI = 1.0e5 m, uNormSI = 5.0e4
m/s), but with B 100x weaker than the d_i ~ v_A ~ 1 scaling: n = 5 /cc,
B = 0.0522 nT, so v_A_code ~ 0.01 and the advection CFL is
U_code*dt_code/dx = 0.2*0.01/0.2 = 0.01.

#INITFROMSWMF
F                       initFromSWMF

#GEOMETRY
-3.2                    xMin  [code units; Lx = 6.4 d_i]
 3.2                    xMax
-0.4                    yMin  (single cell -- true 1D; only x is resolved)
 0.4                    yMax
-0.05                   zMin
 0.05                   zMax

#NCELL
32                      nCellX
1                       nCellY
1                       nCellZ

#MAXBLOCKSIZE
64                      maxBlockSizeX
1                       maxBlockSizeY
1                       maxBlockSizeZ

#PERIODICITY
T                       isPeriodicX
T                       isPeriodicY
T                       isPeriodicZ

Standard Maxwell/GMRES solver disabled; use the Ohm's-law + Faraday hybrid
field advance instead.
#SOLVEEM
F                       solveEM

#HYBRIDPIC
T                       useHybridPIC

Hall term OFF -- the SIMPLEST Ohm's law (E = -U_i x B only). With this flag the
(J x B)/rho term in update_E_hybrid is skipped entirely.
#HALLTERM
F                       useHallTerm

Resistive and electron-pressure-gradient terms OFF (0.0) so the only remaining
E-field source is the convection term -U_i x B.
#RESISTIVITY
0.0                     etaResistivity  [m^2/s, SI magnetic diffusivity]

#ELECTRONTEMPERATURE
0.0                     electronTemperature  [eV]
1.0                     electronGamma
1.0                     electronDensity0

NO sub-cycling: with the Hall term off there is no stiff Hall-whistler mode, so a
single field update per coarse dt is stable and sufficient. nHallSubcycle = 1
keeps the field solver at its cheapest.
#HALLSUBCYCLE
1                       nHallSubcycle

Digital-filter smoothing of the ion moments (rho, rho*U) before the Ohm's law.
This low-passes the PIC shot noise whose time-integration by Faraday produces
the spurious uniform-equilibrium magnetic-energy drift seen without it. The
filter conserves the domain mean, so the uniform free-stream is preserved.
#SMOOTHMOMENTS
T                       doSmoothMoments
3                       nSmoothMoments
0.5                     coefSmoothMoments

Time-centred (predictor-corrector / Crank-Nicolson) Faraday sub-step. Combined
with the moment smoothing this removes the spurious noise drift: the trapezoidal
B update is neutral for oscillatory modes, so the PIC shot noise is no longer
integrated un-damped. thetaB = 0.5 is the standard Crank-Nicolson / Heun scheme.
#CENTEREDB
T                       useCenteredB
0.5                     thetaB

Single kinetic ion species (q = m = 1); the electron is an implicit
neutralizing massless fluid, so no electron particle species is present.
#PLASMA
1                       nSpecies
1.0                     mass
1.0                     charge

#TESTCASE
ConvectionWave

#UNIFORMSTATE
5.0                     rho [amu/cc]   Species 0: ions (n = 5 /cc)
10.0                    ux [km/s]      bulk flow that advects the transverse wave (U_code = 0.2)
0.0                     uy [km/s]
0.0                     uz [km/s]
10000.0                 T [K]
5.2195e-11              bx [T]       weak PASSIVE guide field Bx0 (B_code ~ 0.01, v_A << U)
0.0                     by [T]
0.0                     bz [T]
0.0                     ex [V/m]
0.0                     ey [V/m]
0.0                     ez [V/m]

TESTCASE ConvectionWave -- seeds a transverse (By, Bz) wave via
fill_hybrid_wave(0.2) (B1 = 0.2*Bx0) with NO velocity perturbation, so the
initial field is a rigid transverse wave that is advected by the uniform bulk
flow ux (convection term only; Hall/resistivity/electron-PG are OFF).

#TIMESTEPPING
T                       useFixedDt
0.1                     dt

#NORMALIZATION
1.0e5                   lNormSI   [m]   (tNorm = lNormSI/uNormSI = 2.0 s)
5.0e4                   uNormSI   [m/s] (weak-B test: v_A_code ~ 0.01, NOT 1)

#MONITOR
50                      dnReport

#SAVELOG
10                      dnSavePic
10                      dnSavePT

#PARTICLES
1000                    nParticle per cell in X
1                       nParticle per cell in Y
1                       nParticle per cell in Z

#SAVEPLOT
1                       nPlot
z=0 fluid ascii pic     plotString
-1                      dn          step-based saving disabled (time-based only)
16.0                    dt
1                       dx
Bx By Bz Ex Ey Ez       varName

#STOP
-1                      MaxIter
64.0                    TimeMax

#RUN
